          "type": "see",
          "family": "ኸ"
        },
        {
          "type": "rule",
          "title": "ኸ is another h",
          "text": "ኸ says h too, just like ሀ. Amharic has several letters for the same sound — more of them in week 6."
        },
        {
          "type": "rule",
          "title": "Add a w",
          "text": "Many letters have one extra form that adds a w sound: ቀ → ቋ qwa, ገ → ጓ gwa, ከ → ኳ kwa, ለ → ሏ lwa. You'll see them in words like ቋንቋ (language)."
        },
